		{
			"id":"cc84e9c609042956",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# borg\n### PREDATORY CONSUMER\nangry mammal with tusks\nattacks using a charge ability, which destroys terrain\nattacks animals with similar mass\nhunts animals with lesser mass",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-6010,
			"y":6210,
			"width":360,
			"height":280
		},
		{
			"id":"2a1027d88103d458",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"add ability/hud support for MODIFIER key\n\nhud smartly switching ability icons when MODIFIER key is held down\n\nability will have to have two different icons as well\n\ndefine a fallback texture for no icon",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5120,
			"y":5840,
			"width":460,
			"height":210
		},
		{
			"id":"5f427823f767688a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# moving makes ichor deplete faster!\n\nthis will be hooked up using the inputcomponent probably\n\nichorcomponent <- inputcomponent",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-5100,
			"y":6455,
			"width":300,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"2db3659f6bf6b8ac",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# spawn wave mechanics\n- [ ] define waves of creatures to spawn in a level.\n- [ ] the player must kill most of the creatures (25%) to spawn the next wave.\n- [ ] creatures are given a point value in a dictionary and then the wave manager will greedily spawn in entities at random from the dictionary until points are exhausted or no entities can be afforded.\n- [ ] creatures are spawned in random locations all over the map\n- [ ] creatures are not spawned altogether instantly, but at random intervals within a single time span\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1180,
			"y":5830,
			"width":320,
			"height":420
		},
		{
			"id":"fbb090e984717ecd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# player goal\n1. kill all creatures to advance to the next level\n2. survive (do not run out of ichor or you will starve)\n3. continue on as far as possible",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1180,
			"y":6290,
			"width":260,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"9b3ce986d0a48177",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# generate new level\nWAVER must communicate with the game interface to generate new levels when all waves are complete (and all creatures are killed).",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1180,
			"y":6530,
			"width":260,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"a249a2384311de8d",
			"type":"text",
