		{
			"id":"85818d0aeeb77618",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n| cost | enemy behavior                                                      | ability                                       |\n| ---- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| 50   | attacks nearby creatures                                            | simple swipe                                  |\n|      | shoots projectiles in an axis                                       | shoot a projectile towards movement direction |\n|      | picks a target, shoots explosive fireball, teleports                | shoot a fireball                              |\n|      | if attacked, sets a timer to detonation                             |                                               |\n|      | swallows creatures. if killed, expels out all swallowed creatures   |                                               |\n|      | wanders around quickly                                              |                                               |\n|      | worm that divides when cut in half                                  |                                               |\n|      | chooses a home, wanders around and steals food to bring to its home |                                               |\n|      | hops great distances and pounds the ground dealing damage           |                                               |\n|      | charges through terrain and flattens walls                          |                                               |\n|      | builds walls                                                        |                                               |\n|      | plants 3 explosive barrels                                          |                                               |\n|      | undergoes mitosis when hit                                          |                                               |\n|      | moves through walls and spits fireballs                             |                                               |\n|      | creates smaller versions of itself to charge at creatures           |                                               |\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1560,
			"y":4570,
			"width":1180,
			"height":560
		},
		{
			"id":"d3c2ab3e3e9e6fee",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n| Behavior Class | Description                                                           |\n| -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| PASSIVE        | Does not attack other creatures OR flees when nearby other creatures. |\n| REACTIVE       | Only retaliates if provoked.                                          |\n| PREDATORY      | Actively hunts other creatures to satiate itself.                     |\n| FERAL          | Violent towards other creatures.                                      |\n| ALOOF          | Does not care about other creatures.                                  |\n\n| Consumer Type | Description                                                 |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| AMBIENT       | Ichor is replenished passively over time given a condition. |\n| PROXIMITY     | Ichor is replenished when nearby a specific entity.         |\n| CONSUMER      | Ichor is replenished by consuming entities                  |\n| ESOTERIC      | Ichor is replenished through unconventional means.          |\n| EXEMPT        | Does not have ichor.                                        |\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1560,
			"y":5170,
			"width":720,
			"height":480
		},
		{
			"id":"2699fe0e3c46687f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"what i absolutely need within 2 weeks:\n- wave-based spawner\n\t- can detect how many enemies it has spawned versus how many are alive\n\t- when creatures_alive_count reaches a bottom threshold, summon a new wave\n\t- spawn creatures based on a point system?\n\t- how are creatures spawned? creatures need to be assigned point values i think\n\t- assign number of waves and point value upon board creation\n- assign creatures a point value?\n- three basic fun creatures\n- more gui and animation for changing level\n- fit abilities with possible upgrades\n\t- merge abilities?\n\t- base power increase\n- generate different size of levels",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-800,
			"y":5170,
			"width":460,
			"height":520
		},
		{
			"id":"ebb5cb4880db2686",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"simpler gameplay loop:\n\n1. enter board (level)\n2. win by surviving multiple waves\n\t1. kill all creatures in a wave\n\t2. maintain ichor/survive\n3. beat the final wave/boss fight\n4. gain new abilities/powers or upgrade\n5. new random board is generated",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":5170,
			"width":380,
			"height":380
		},
		{
			"id":"cddc2fe219132dc6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# fun\nkeep the player challenged, not bored, not too hard\njuicy feedback\nplayer choice",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":560,
			"y":5170,
			"width":440,
			"height":480
		},
		{
			"id":"da46c0accba0e1f4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# blom bulb\n### PASSIVE AMBIENT\nflowering plant\nshort lifespan (1 min)\ngrows an edible fruit over time\nthe fruit will create another bulb if left on the ground for some time\n\n> done 09/13/26",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1100,
			"y":7010,
			"width":300,
			"height":280
		},
		{
			"id":"22ff6807b5d45222",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"GET THE DAMN INTERACTOR WORKING",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":780,
			"y":7150,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2c5d06a364b13a19",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"creatures, when killed, turn into food which can be eaten to gain some ichor.\n\nichor should have a `try_steal()` function that attempts to steal ichor but if the entity has none it fails and if the actor has max then it fails. \n\non death food drop component!\n\n---\n- [x] note the ichor of the creature when it died\n- [ ] specify thresholds that must be passed to spawn specific foods\n- [x] food dropped must have the ichor value (or less, random) of the creature that dropped it\n\n> done 09-14-2026",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":300,
			"y":7270,
			"width":540,
			"height":435
		},
		{
			"id":"26f20e5242ee4451",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# blimble\n### PASSIVE CONSUMER\nsmall bouncy white creature\nlikes to be near other blimbles\neats plants or fruit\nruns away from larger animals",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":930,
			"y":7348,
			"width":320,
			"height":280
		},
		{
			"id":"701228c35defd60d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"actual competent entityspawner mechanic:\nentities won't be spawned using their name directly, instead entities will use the entitytag system to define an esoterica archetype for the entity!\n\n> done 09-01-2026\n\nso we made these changes\n- made the registries!\n\t- `EntityRegistry` got fitted with new code that indexes all registered enemies and organizes them into categories based on their `CreatureArchetype`.\n\t- `AccessoryArchetypeRegistry` which registers all `AccessoryArchetypes`, needed for the Anthurium to pick which accessory to grow based on its current `Esoterica` value.\n- `SpawnTable` resource defines weights for each category in `CreatureArchetype` and utilizes the `EntityRegistry` to pick an entity id (`StringName`) based on a weighted intersection of all the categories.\n\t- `SpawnTableSpawnerComponent` holds a `SpawnTable` and calls its function.\n- `spawn_portal(pos: Vector2, spawn_table: SpawnTable)` is now a method in `EntityManager`",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":5825,
			"width":500,
			"height":540
		},
		{
			"id":"e3b1c1051b07e5e1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"hunger isn't really implemented yet.\n\nentities that have ichor components should slowly lose their health if they have 0% ichor.\n\n> done 09-01-2026\n\nmade these changes\n- literally just made ichor and health interface with each other because i dont wanna bother with being clever\n- ichor now decays over time and when it reaches zero, health will slowly tick down.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":840,
			"y":5825,
			"width":460,
			"height":320
		},
		{
			"id":"019b01a78a3edd79",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"make explosion entity that is spawned in on an explosion\\\n\n> done 09-04-2026",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":840,
			"y":6230,
			"width":260,
			"height":135
		},
		{
			"id":"5337b9a1c263e641",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"a main menu\n\nthe main menu should just be an already initialized game without the player\n\n(the camera should choose to focus on a randomly picked entity on the map)\n\nthere will only be an option to play again or turn on and off the shaders. (this is because this will be a demo copy)\n\n> done 09-04-2026\n\n---\n\n- [x] it is written in `AppController` `enum AppStatus { MENU, GAME, GAMEOVER }`.\n- [x] **MENU** should have the main menu open and visible with hand visible and able to select various interactableui elements.\n- [x] title, play, shader settings. (this is a demo copy so no quit button)\n\nmake this:\n- UIStage (simply registers all of its interactableUI)\n\t- InteractableUI (multiple of these, triggers an event when the hand activates it)\n\nwhere a method on `Hand` `switch_to_stage(stage: UIStage)` correctly moves the hand to the first element in the stage. this will be useful for navigating through different menu screens.\n\nessentially, activate a new game but do not spawn the player.\n\nensure that the hand always follows the element in space that it has selected.\n\n**GAME** is when the player is spawned and fully in control. ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":6415,
			"width":710,
			"height":680
		},
		{
			"id":"54af69f0cd6ae0a0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"get z-axis working\n\n#### okay\n- [x] z-axis needs to connect to hitbox and change its layer based on z-axis value\n- [x] z-axis must connect to ability manager\n- [x] ability should have a field `affected by z-axis`\n- [x] so that abilities that have hurtboxes can change hurtbox layer based on z-axis\n- [x] physicscomponent needs to connect to z-axis; collisions should not happen between entities that are 5 z units apart (?)\n\n- [x] z-axis needs a reference to sprite `scale` to generate a shadow of a particular size\n- [x] shadow should decrease in size the higher up z value is\n\n- [x] jumping over terrain\n\n- [x] shadows\n- [x] jumping\n\n- [x] verify that the hitbox/hurtbox levels work by making a flying entity",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1070,
			"y":6415,
			"width":590,
			"height":510
		},
